    hr_notes: "Standard terms\n• Fixed CTC ₹15,000 a month on the morning shift, plus the evening/night shift allowance; no negotiation (L8/L7 hiring standard, Oct 2026)\n• Relationship Associates are paid above the base L8 figure because the role needs client-handling skill\n• Women are rostered on the morning shift only\n• Joining only on the Monday nearest the 7th, 14th, 21st or 28th; the next working day if that Monday is a holiday\n• Police clearance certificate and the background-verification checklist are compulsory before joining\n• Training-month pay, security deposit, probation and notice are set in the offer letter as per the current hiring standard\n\nWhat to test in the interview\n• Third-party money: a client says a friend will pay, or wants the payout sent to a relative. They should stop, raise it with the Relationship Executive in the same interaction, and accept no third-party payout\n• Report, don't filter: a friendly regular client suddenly makes a much larger payment from a newly added account. They should report it exactly as observed, not judge it; a concern that proves unfounded is never an error\n• Composure: role-play an angry client pushing to skip a document request. They should stay calm, hold the step and raise the pressure with the Relationship Executive at once\n• Recording: read out a short client call with a new mobile number and a payout-timing question; they should log the change at once and promise no payout time\n• Night shifts: confirm they can work the rotation, including nights and weekends\n\nKeep in mind\n• Strong fresh graduates may be considered for the Purchase Side only; delete that clause for a Sales Side opening\n• No Associate handles client accounts before completing KYC and AML training and certification\n\nSource: JD Compendium v4.2, BVT/HR/JD/2026/001",
