    position_id: "1bfa5f33-7143-4c7e-b648-c10facdfe8b0",
    title: "KYC Associate",
    jd_reference: "BVT/HR/JD/2026/004",
    summary: "Verify who BlynkEx's clients are through document checks and live video KYC, review transaction monitoring alerts on your shift, and keep every KYC record complete and audit-ready. The role rotates across shifts, including nights, and what counts is what you catch, not how many files you clear.",
    description: "As a KYC Associate you help the company know who its clients are and what they actually do. You verify identity before a client transacts, run live video KYC sessions, review monitoring alerts and keep every KYC record complete and easy to retrieve.\n\nYou are the first line of our compliance checks, so care matters more than speed. You work rotational shifts, including the night shift.\n\nWhat you'll do\n• Verify identity, address and, for business clients, constitutional documents, checking each one closely for authenticity and consistency\n• Run live video KYC sessions, checking original documents and recording each session accurately\n• Carry out sanctions, politically exposed person and adverse media screening, apply risk categorisation and start enhanced due diligence where needed\n• Review every transaction monitoring alert on your shift and record a clear written observation on each one\n• Refer anything unusual, or anything you are unsure about, to your KYC Executive straight away\n• Keep each client's KYC record complete and current in our systems, including periodic KYC reviews and the reason for every decision\n• Treat all client information as strictly confidential, including whether a client's file is under review\n• Close each shift with a short report and a clear handover of open alerts and pending files\n\nWho you'll work with\nYou'll report to the KYC Executive on your shift, in a team led by the shift Internal Compliance Officer, and work most closely with the Operations and Client Relations teams.",
    requirements: "• Graduate in any discipline\n• One year or more in KYC, onboarding, document verification or transaction monitoring; strong fresh graduates may also be considered\n• A sharp eye for inconsistencies between documents, and the patience to look for them on every file\n• Clear spoken Hindi and English, and the composure to run a video session with someone you have not met\n• Disciplined record-keeping and accurate written observations\n• Willing to work rotational shifts, including the night shift\n• Able to clear background and reference verification\n\nGood to have\n• KYC or AML experience at a bank, NBFC, fintech or payments company\n• Familiarity with sanctions and adverse media screening tools\n• Experience of video-based customer identification\n• Working knowledge of KYC and AML rules, including the PMLA framework\n\nYou'll do well here if you\n• Are comfortable being the person who slows things down\n• Escalate rather than assume, even when the answer is probably fine\n• Stay unmoved by urgency, seniority or a client's frustration\n• Handle sensitive client information with complete discretion",
