    hr_notes: "Standard terms\n• Fixed CTC ₹13,600 a month on the morning shift, plus the evening/night shift allowance; no negotiation (L8/L7 hiring standard, Oct 2026)\n• For a client-facing video KYC opening, title the job \"KYC Associate – Video Process\"; its morning-shift CTC is the same as a Relationship Associate's (₹15,000)\n• Women are rostered on the morning shift only\n• Joining only on the Monday nearest the 7th, 14th, 21st or 28th; the next working day if that Monday is a holiday\n• Police clearance certificate and the background-verification checklist are compulsory before joining\n• Training-month pay, security deposit, probation and notice are set in the offer letter as per the current hiring standard\n\nWhat to test in the interview\n• Documents: show two documents with a small name or date mismatch; they should spot it and refer it\n• Video KYC: role-play a session where the client is prompted off-camera; they should stop it and refer it\n• Pressure: an Operations colleague wants a file cleared fast because a large client transaction is waiting. The right answer is to state the status, not negotiate it, and report the request to the KYC Executive\n• Confidentiality: in a video KYC the client asks why their transaction has not gone through. The right answer reveals nothing about any review or referral\n• Night shifts: confirm they can work the full rotation, including nights\n\nKeep in mind\n• This role must carry no throughput incentive and no measure linked to transaction volume, transaction value or clearance rate; never offer one to a candidate\n• For a \"KYC Associate – Video Process\" opening, set the salary field and the first \"What we offer\" line to ₹15,000 and use that title in the line, before publishing\n\nSource: JD Compendium v4.2, BVT/HR/JD/2026/004",
