    description: "As an HR Associate you are the working hands behind hiring, onboarding and employee records, supporting the HR Executive and the HR Manager. You are also the first point of contact for routine questions from staff.\n\nThis is a day-shift role. Pay, performance and discipline sit with the HR Manager, so you answer from written policy and refer anything else rather than guess.\n\nWhat you'll do\n• Post approved vacancies on job portals as supplied, screen applications against the stated criteria, and shortlist with reasons\n• Call candidates to check fit, availability, how soon they can join, location and shift willingness, sharing only approved information\n• Schedule interviews, confirm attendance before each slot, and keep the recruitment tracker and call log up to date\n• Follow up on documents, references and background verification before an offer, and stay in touch with candidates until they join\n• Answer routine questions on leave, attendance and documents from written policy, log each one, and refer the rest to the HR Executive\n• Maintain employee records and the HRMS, keep personnel files complete, and compile attendance and leave data for payroll\n• Prepare joining kits, schedule induction and confirm it is complete before a joiner starts live work\n• Coordinate assets and system access for joiners, and document collection, asset return and clearance for leavers\n\nWho you'll work with\nYou report to the HR Executive, in the HR team led by the HR Manager. You speak with candidates, interviewers and employees every day.",
